From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:28:47 -0400
Subject: toolbar: the address row hides with the sidebar; shift-cmd-D shows it
 on its own

A per-window AddressRow, owned by the Space model beside the page colour,
answers BrowserView::IsToolbarVisible: with the sidebar collapsed and
stedding.toolbar.hide_with_sidebar on, the row hides and the content card
takes the full height with its gutters; a localhost page always keeps the
row; shift-cmd-D (IDC_STEDDING_TOGGLE_ADDRESS_ROW, an id kept out of
chrome_command_ids.h to spare the rebuild) overrides the rule for the
window until the sidebar changes. The setting is a toggle under the
sidebar rows, the chord is in the shortcut reference and the bar's
actions (docs/features/toolbar.md T8, T10-T12; T9 dropped, T13 the second
half).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 3, R6-25: Arc hides the bar with the
sidebar.
Removable when: Chromium's vertical tab strip hides the toolbar with the
strip.
